# The mutual case: neither declaration holds itself, and together they do.
#
# One diagnostic, not two, because a cycle is one mistake ("one mistake, one
# message" — `types/lower.rs`). The note carries the cycle as a path with field
# names and lines, because BOTH edges are legal repair sites: the author may put
# `A.b` in an array or `B.a` in one, and a message naming a single field silently
# would be arbitrary advice dressed as help.
#
# Go arrived here by being told. Its old `cmd/compile` printed only `invalid
# recursive type T2` for exactly this shape and that was filed as a bug (golang
# #41575, "not as helpful as go/types"); the path form is what replaced it.
#
# The cycle is normalised to start at the lowest declaration index, so the
# reported path does not depend on which declaration the walk entered from.
# Without that, the message would change when the walk's entry point changed and
# this `.expected` would rot for a reason having nothing to do with the program.

record A
    b: B

record B
    a: A    #~ no_size

function main()
    print(1)
